----

_init ==
    /\ recep = _TETrace[1].recep
    /\ comm = _TETrace[1].comm
    /\ upend = _TETrace[1].upend
    /\ pend = _TETrace[1].pend
    /\ tos = _TETrace[1].tos
    /\ view = _TETrace[1].view
    /\ hqr = _TETrace[1].hqr
    /\ seal = _TETrace[1].seal
    /\ rows = _TETrace[1].rows
    /\ votes = _TETrace[1].votes
    /\ props = _TETrace[1].props
    /\ info = _TETrace[1].info
    /\ hvr = _TETrace[1].hvr
    /\ lastprop = _TETrace[1].lastprop
----

_next ==
    /\ \E i,j \in DOMAIN _TETrace:
        /\ \/ /\ j = i + 1
              /\ i = TLCGet("level")
        /\ recep  = _TETrace[i].recep
        /\ recep' = _TETrace[j].recep
        /\ comm  = _TETrace[i].comm
        /\ comm' = _TETrace[j].comm
        /\ upend  = _TETrace[i].upend
        /\ upend' = _TETrace[j].upend
        /\ pend  = _TETrace[i].pend
        /\ pend' = _TETrace[j].pend
        /\ tos  = _TETrace[i].tos
        /\ tos' = _TETrace[j].tos
        /\ view  = _TETrace[i].view
        /\ view' = _TETrace[j].view
        /\ hqr  = _TETrace[i].hqr
        /\ hqr' = _TETrace[j].hqr
        /\ seal  = _TETrace[i].seal
        /\ seal' = _TETrace[j].seal
        /\ rows  = _TETrace[i].rows
        /\ rows' = _TETrace[j].rows
        /\ votes  = _TETrace[i].votes
        /\ votes' = _TETrace[j].votes
        /\ props  = _TETrace[i].props
        /\ props' = _TETrace[j].props
        /\ info  = _TETrace[i].info
        /\ info' = _TETrace[j].info
        /\ hvr  = _TETrace[i].hvr
        /\ hvr' = _TETrace[j].hvr
        /\ lastprop  = _TETrace[i].lastprop
        /\ lastprop' = _TETrace[j].lastprop

\* Uncomment the ASSUME below to write the states of the error trace
\* to the given file in Json format. Note that you can pass any tuple
\* to `JsonSerialize`. For example, a sub-sequence of _TETrace.
    \* ASSUME
    \*     LET J == INSTANCE Json
    \*         IN J!JsonSerialize("EpochTransition_TTrace_1794417744.json", _TETrace)

=============================================================================

 Note that you can extract this module `EpochTransition_TEExpression`
  to a dedicated file to reuse `expression` (the module in the 
  dedicated `EpochTransition_TEExpression.tla` file takes precedence 
  over the module `EpochTransition_TEExpression` below).

---- MODULE EpochTransition_TEExpression ----
EXTENDS Sequences, TLCExt, Toolbox, Naturals, TLC, EpochTransition

expression == 
    [
        \* To hide variables of the `EpochTransition` spec from the error trace,
        \* remove the variables below.  The trace will be written in the order
        \* of the fields of this record.
        recep |-> recep
        ,comm |-> comm
        ,upend |-> upend
        ,pend |-> pend
        ,tos |-> tos
        ,view |-> view
        ,hqr |-> hqr
        ,seal |-> seal
        ,rows |-> rows
        ,votes |-> votes
        ,props |-> props
        ,info |-> info
        ,hvr |-> hvr
        ,lastprop |-> lastprop
        
        \* Put additional constant-, state-, and action-level expressions here:
        \* ,_stateNumber |-> _TEPosition
        \* ,_recepUnchanged |-> recep = recep'
        
        \* Format the `recep` variable as Json value.
        \* ,_recepJson |->
        \*     LET J == INSTANCE Json
        \*     IN J!ToJson(recep)
        
        \* Lastly, you may build expressions over arbitrary sets of states by
        \* leveraging the _TETrace operator.  For example, this is how to
        \* count the number of times a spec variable changed up to the current
        \* state in the trace.
        \* ,_recepModCount |->
        \*     LET F[s \in DOMAIN _TETrace] ==
        \*         IF s = 1 THEN 0
        \*         ELSE IF _TETrace[s].recep # _TETrace[s-1].recep
        \*             THEN 1 + F[s-1] ELSE F[s-1]
        \*     IN F[_TEPosition - 1]
    ]

=============================================================================



Parsing and semantic processing can take forever if the trace below is long.
 In this case, it is advised to uncomment the module below to deserialize the
 trace from a generated binary file.

\*
\*---- MODULE EpochTransition_TETrace ----
\*EXTENDS IOUtils, TLC, EpochTransition
\*
\*trace == IODeserialize("EpochTransition_TTrace_1794417744.bin", TRUE)
\*
\*=============================================================================
\*

---- MODULE EpochTransition_TETrace ----
EXTENDS TLC, EpochTransition

